<stack style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 3">
  <head>
    <!-- THE DECORATION LAYER, AND THE REASON IT IS DATA.
         Everything a slide carries besides the screen and the headline - a logo, a mascot, a
         rating badge, a feature chip, a callout ring over a UI detail - is one row of a JSON
         array. An agent composing a screenshot set therefore writes DATA into the shot
         profile; it never authors markup. That is the difference between "the AI can use the
         tool" and "the AI can use the tool only if it writes DSX correctly every time".

         Each row: {kind, x, y, ...}. `x`/`y` are percentages of the slide, so a decoration
         means the same thing at every device size.

         WHY EIGHT FIXED SLOTS AND NOT A <list>. A bound list was the obvious shape and it does
         not work here: `.dsx-list > *` resolves its rows to `position: relative`, so every
         absolutely-placed decoration collapsed into flex flow and stacked down the left edge.
         Measured, in a probe: computed `position: relative`, `top: 0px` on every row, against
         a control pair outside a list that placed exactly. Eight is also the honest ceiling -
         a slide carrying more than eight decorations is not a screenshot, it is a collage.

         WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY WILL NOT DRAW, and it matters more than what it will: there is
         no store-award badge. "Editors' Choice" is a real Google Play award with its own
         branding, and "Top Rated" reads as one; both stores' metadata policies ban implying an
         editorial endorsement you do not have, and it is a trademark problem besides. A badge
         here carries a claim the customer can substantiate - their real rating, their real
         install count, a feature actually in the build, a press quote actually received. -->
    <attribute as="items" sample="[]"/>
  </head>

  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 0" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[0] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 1" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[1] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 2" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[2] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 3" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[3] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 4" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[4] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 5" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[5] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 6" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[6] }}"/>
  <ShotDecorItem visible-if="dsx.attribute.items.length > 7" item="{{ dsx.attribute.items[7] }}"/>
</stack>
